{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_10a",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "included a waiting period ≥ 4 weeks for the WLCG, no-treatment group or cohort of patients who ultimately received outpatient psychotherapy; reported ED-specific PROs, measured using the Children's Eating Attitudes Test (chEAT) [73], Eating Disorder Examination-Questionnaire (EDEQ) [74] or EDE-Q 6.0 [75], for all study groups separately; and reported these PROs for a minimum of two time points: (1) at or near the time of initial consultation, diagnostic workup, or study enrolment (baseline), and (2) at least once at a subsequent time point (i.e. at intervention start and/or at follow-up).",
      "reason": "Outcome domains are partially listed (e.g., ED-specific PROs measured by chEAT/EDE-Q and the EDE-Q items including Global Score, subscales, and core behavior items), but a clear structured list of all outcome domains sought with explicit domain definitions is not fully provided in the retrieved text."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "reported these PROs for a minimum of two time points: (1) at or near the time of initial consultation, diagnostic workup, or study enrolment (baseline), and (2) at least once at a subsequent time point (i.e. at intervention start and/or at follow-up).",
      "reason": "The measurement time frame for outcome assessment is specified as baseline and at least one subsequent post-waiting time point (intervention start and/or follow-up)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not state whether all compatible results within each outcome domain were sought (e.g., across all measures/time points/analyses) or how comprehensiveness was handled."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This conditional requirement depends on whether not all compatible results were sought; the retrieved evidence does not describe whether result selection was necessary or, if so, the selection process."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "During the work process, the eligibility criteria have been amended once to ensure precision, clarity, and reproducibility. Additionally, the eligible patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs) have been specified to enhance comparability between the individual studies. This specification was made in accordance with the ICHOM recommendations [33] to follow international consensus and ensure participation of persons with lived experience in the decision-making process.",
      "reason": "The evidence reports amendments to eligibility criteria and specification of PROMs with stated rationales (precision/clarity/reproducibility; enhance comparability; align with ICHOM to follow consensus and include lived experience). However, it is not explicit that these amendments changed outcome-domain inclusion/definitions/importance specifically beyond the PROM specification."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e6",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not describe changes to processes for selecting results within eligible outcome domains (including any rationales for such changes)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e7",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Generic PROs of well-being or functioning (measured using the KIDSCREEN-10 [85] or the WHO Disability Assessment Schedule 2.0 [86]), other mental healthrelated PROs, i.e. measures of anxiety, depression, and suicidal ideation..., as well as ED-specific QoL and social functioning (measured using the Clinical Impairment Assessment [91]) were eligible as secondary outcomes, but not required for inclusion.",
      "reason": "The evidence indicates prioritisation between mandatory ED-specific PRO outcomes (required) and generic/other outcomes as secondary and not required. However, it does not clearly state which outcomes were considered most important *for interpreting the conclusions* or provide a rationale for prioritising the specific most-important outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 62
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_10b",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "A standardised data extraction form was developed and piloted on a small number of studies to ensure consistency across studies and between reviewers. Extracted data items are displayed in Additional file 5.",
      "reason": "The review states that extracted data items are presented (Additional file 5), but the evidence provided here does not list and define all the “other variables” that were sought; it only indicates the existence/location of the item list and describes some specific variables (e.g., funding sources, conflicts of interest, EDE-Q means/SDs) without fully enumerating and defining them."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "For Arcelus et al. [104], post-waiting means and post-waiting SDs were unavailable and could not be obtained by contacting the corresponding author. Post-waiting means were derived by adding the reported mean difference (MD) to the pre-waiting mean. As proposed by Morris [105] and Morris and DeShon [106], SDs in pre- and post-test populations can be assumed equal. However, to increase the precision we approximated post-waiting SDs by multiplying the pre-waiting SD by the average proportional change in SDs from pre to post observed in the remaining included studies.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly describes assumptions and derivation methods used when post-waiting information was missing/unavailable (deriving means from MD, assuming pre/post SD equality, and approximating SDs via proportional change)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The evidence provided does not cite any tool used to determine which data items to collect. While it mentions that a standardised data extraction form was developed and piloted, it does not explicitly describe citing a tool for deciding which data items were collected."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 62
}

{
